# L §8.1 (tally 2.3, #247; P7): `missing(pnl[w])` with a window for a key is `false`, as with any hole key,
# never the window's hole; pinned, the row's answer. Before: the window's hole (`a key`).
=== m.tally
model miss
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
input pnl[d in days]: num
input w: date
def mk: bool
  rule base v v1 = false
  rule no_record beats base v v1 = true when missing(pnl[w])
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pnl[2026-03-02] = 1 "s"
  w = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-03) "s"
ask k: mk
ask k_in: mk with w = 2026-03-02
ask k_out: mk with w = 2026-03-03
=== expect
k: false
  cut 2026-12-31
k_in: false
  pinned: w = 2026-03-02
  cut 2026-12-31
k_out: true
  missing record counted by v1
  pinned: w = 2026-03-03
  cut 2026-12-31
